Not claimed: any lower bound on `L` from the tree, any kill, any ceiling on `D`. §3 exhibits an explicitly **satisfiable** arithmetic solution at `(64,48), N=4` — `ORTHO` alone empties nothing; the content has to come from the proximity structure of a real cluster. That is why the decisive move is Card A (six integers on Moh's four survivors), not more theory.

